<speak>
<s>This is your Jumu'ah briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">12062026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Iran has mined the waters around Kharg Island and ringed its main oil terminal with air defenses, daring the United States to make good on Donald Trump's vow to seize it.</s> <s>Kharg handles the overwhelming majority of Iran's crude exports, and analysts warn American long-range weapons stocks are already depleted after weeks of strikes.</s> <s>Whether Washington risks the casualties such an assault would demand... no one yet knows.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A Seoul court has added thirty years to former President Yoon Suk Yeol's sentence, ruling he ordered drones into North Korea's capital in October twenty twenty-four.</s> <s>The judges found he engineered the provocation deliberately, hoping Pyongyang would retaliate and hand him a pretext to declare martial law.</s> <s>It's a rare verdict naming a head of state's attempt to manufacture a foreign crisis to seize power at home.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>As the World Cup opened in Mexico City, hundreds of mothers known as madres buscadoras marched to the stadium gates carrying photographs of the disappeared.</s> <s>Nearly one hundred thirty-five thousand Mexicans are missing, and the families chose the tournament's global glare to demand the state account for them.</s> <s>They sprayed the word desaparecidos across the capital's monuments... a grief the celebration couldn't drown out.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Rapid Support Forces drones struck mourners gathered at a cemetery in El Obeid, killing twenty-three civilians in a single attack.</s> <s>Across Sudan this week the group's drones have killed at least thirty people, the Emergency Lawyers Group reports, as the war grinds through another brutal year.</s> <s>The United Nations now warns that bridge damage near Delling could sever humanitarian routes just as the rains begin.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>France's digital interference agency has named an Israeli firm, BlackCore, as the hand behind smear campaigns against pro-Palestinian politicians.</s> <s>The operation reached into French local elections and votes in the United States and three other countries, investigators say, though no sponsor has been identified.</s> <s>A commercial disinformation vendor reaching into several democracies at once... and still no one knows who paid for it.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Damascus is quietly courting Gulf states to loosen its dependence on Turkey, the patron that intervened in Idlib back in twenty twenty and remains its main security guarantor.</s> <s>Syria's new rulers are renegotiating a relationship the world assumed was simple patronage, leveraging Ankara's own needs to claw back room to maneuver.</s> <s>No alternative arrangement has been announced, leaving the balance between the two capitals unsettled.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Pakistan has diverted more than nine hundred billion rupees from its provinces to the federal center, freezing provincial development spending past this fiscal year.</s> <s>Three shocks forced the move, the government concedes — trade disruption, devastating floods, and the oil-price fallout of the Iran war.</s> <s>It's a quiet recentralization of money and power, and the provinces are the ones told to wait.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Vietnam has passed its first halal certification law, treating the standard not as a religious formality but as trade infrastructure.</s> <s>Hanoi is competing directly with Malaysia and Indonesia for Islamic export lanes and Muslim tourism, markets worth trillions across the Organisation of Islamic Cooperation.</s> <s>The law still requires building the certification bodies from scratch, so whether Vietnam can deliver is the real test.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Paraguay has seized a premium cannabis shipment heading south from Miami, a small bust that marks a striking reversal.</s> <s>Legalization across North America has crushed wholesale prices to around one thousand dollars a pound, sending the high-grade product flowing south into Brazil and beyond.</s> <s>Decades of northward trafficking are inverting... and the geography of the drug trade is quietly turning upside down.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s><sub alias="S and P Global">S&P Global</sub> has flagged Africa as the region most exposed to a coming wave of food inflation.</s> <s>Households across much of the continent spend more than forty percent of their income on food, and fertiliser shocks are still working their way into consumer prices months later.</s> <s>Nigerian petrol prices have already climbed twenty-five percent, and food, analysts warn, comes next.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Researchers at Germany's federal materials institute argue the answer to critical-mineral dependence lies upstream, in design itself.</s> <s>Rather than scrambling to secure mines for batteries, turbines, and electronics, they say these products should be built from the start to be recyclable and resource-light.</s> <s>It inverts the usual debate... the bottleneck may not be where we dig, but how we design.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The European Space Agency has handed Italy's Luca Parmitano a seat on Artemis Three, reversing an earlier plan to give it to Germany.</s> <s>His test-pilot background proved decisive after NASA retooled the flight as a low-Earth-orbit test rather than a lunar landing.</s> <s>It's a small window into how the agencies ration who gets to fly — individual qualification quietly overriding national rotation.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Peru's artisanal fishers have grounded their boats, caught between an El Niño that scatters fish stocks and fuel costs that have climbed more than twenty-five percent.</s> <s>Every trip now loses money, and from Peru to the Philippines no relief program has been announced for those absorbing both shocks at once.</s> <s>The ocean that fed coastal communities for generations is, for now, no longer paying its way.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>India's railway minister has promised to rebuild the country's notorious online ticketing system after a student's plea over its broken captcha went public.</s> <s>The state-run platform brokers seats for tens of millions of travelers daily, yet payment crashes and bot-driven seat theft have made it a national source of friction.</s> <s>A new site is pledged by mid-July, though fixing infrastructure this large rarely arrives on schedule.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>The United States Senate Armed Services Committee has killed a proposal to create a sixth military branch for cyber operations, by a single vote, fourteen to thirteen.</s> <s>Senator Kirsten Gillibrand had argued the armed forces need a standing cyber service the way they once needed an air force a century ago.</s> <s>The trillion-dollar defense bill moves on, but the question of who fights the nation's digital wars stays wide open.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>